A||||6||Fformula88||Intermittent rough idle/stalling||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||03-10-2001||11:50 PM||||My 88 Formula V6 ATX idles very rough and stalls when cold about 70% of the time.  The rest of the time it runs perfectly at startup and when cold.  The symptoms go away once the car warms up... after 5-10 minutes.<P>Exactly, when I crank it it fires right up and runs smooth.  A few seconds later it will start to idle more irratically.  If I put it into reverse without giving it a little gas it will stall.  It goes into drive without stalling.  On its worst days it may also stall at the first couple stop signs I reach if I push too hard on the brakes.  It will also be idling very poorly when this happens, but runs fine when given some gas.  Any ideas on what this could be?  Here is what the dealer, my local mechanic, or I have done.<P>New: complete tune up (plugs, wires, cap, rotor, coil, PCV, charcoal canister filter).<BR>EGR Tube,<BR>EGR Valve,<BR>Vacumn lines checked and repaired for leaks<BR>Throttle body cleaned<BR>IAC Valve cleaned<BR>Intake plenum removed and cleaned<P>I hope I haven't missed anything here.  I believe the cat is also bad, but it seems to have plenty of power so I don't think its causing the idle problem.<P>How likely is this to be caused by any of the following... fuel injectors, IAC valve, EGR valve, MAP sensor.  There are no engine codes sets.  Hope you guys can lend some insight!  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||03-11-2001||08:02 PM||||top||||reg||1
Z||000002||daved||03-11-2001||09:03 PM||||88, I would measure the resistance of the MAT sensor (the thermistor mounted on the air cleaner.  Mine measured around 4.27kOhms at 10 Deg C., it varies quite a bit with temperature<BR>Ohms  	  deg f /deg-c<BR>7500 	  40/4<BR>3400	70/20<BR>1800	100/38<BR>450	160/70<BR>185	210/100 <BR>I suggest this because it is one of the things the ECM can't check to see if it's a good signal.  Yours is a tricky problem, hope you find it soon,  Dave ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||03-12-2001||01:37 PM||||Thanks for the advice daved, I'll get on it and try.  Anybody else have a suggestion?  I haven't found a shop that has actually fixed it, though many have tried.  Its becoming very discouraging that I cannot make it run.  I hate to start swapping parts at random since it could get very expensive and not fix the trouble.  Thanks for any insight you may be able to give!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||03-12-2001||11:40 PM||||Just gonna send this to the top one more time...||||reg||1
Z||000005||David Gamache||03-13-2001||11:01 AM||||Since the car starts up ok but stalls when you try to drive it cold and idles better when you give it gas it sounds like a possible faulty cold start injector. It is located on the bottom of the intake near the distributor area.  If you had problems starting up the motor,then I would have thought possibly a fuel related problem like a faulty injector leaking fuel, a check valve in the gas tank leaking back into the tank at night, or a fuel pressure problem. Also poor running fronm the get-go could have been a bad IAC not seating properly and disrupting the air/fuel mix or if the motor  stalled when being put into drive it may have been a TCC in the trans problem. a bad TPS or MAP would probably be likely t cause poor gas milage and poor performance, which does not seem to be the case.  Just my thoughts.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fformula88||03-14-2001||11:32 PM||||Thanks for the input!  I'll look into the cold start injector too.||||reg||1
